api.doc:
holeDirArea(self: meshlib.mrmeshpy.Mesh, e: meshlib.mrmeshpy.EdgeId) -> meshlib.mrmeshpy.Vector3d

computes directed area of the hole specified by one of its edges with no valid left face (left is hole);
if the hole is planar then returned vector is orthogonal to the plane pointing outside and its magnitude is equal to hole area

volume(self: meshlib.mrmeshpy.Mesh, region: meshlib.mrmeshpy.FaceBitSet = None) -> float

returns volume of the object surrounded by given region (or whole mesh if (region) is nullptr);
if the region has holes then each hole will be virtually filled by adding triangles for each edge and the hole's geometrical center

checkValidity(self: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshTopology, cb: meshlib.mrmeshpy.func_bool_from_float = '{}', allVerts: bool = True) -> bool

verifies that all internal data structures are valid;
if allVerts=true then checks in addition that all not-lone edges have valid vertices on both ends

findHoleRepresentiveEdges(self: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshTopology, region: meshlib.mrmeshpy.FaceBitSet = None) -> meshlib.mrmeshpy.std_vector_Id_EdgeTag

returns one edge with no valid left face for every boundary in the mesh;
if region is given, then returned edges must have valid right faces from the region

findNumHoles(self: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshTopology, holeRepresentativeEdges: meshlib.mrmeshpy.EdgeBitSet = None) -> int

returns the number of hole loops in the mesh;
\param holeRepresentativeEdges optional output of the smallest edge id with no valid left face in every hole

findHoleComplicatingFaces(mesh: meshlib.mrmeshpy.Mesh) -> meshlib.mrmeshpy.FaceBitSet

returns all faces that complicate one of mesh holes;
hole is complicated if it passes via one vertex more than once;
deleting such faces simplifies the holes and makes them easier to fill

holeDirArea(topology: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshTopology, points: meshlib.mrmeshpy.VertCoords, e: meshlib.mrmeshpy.EdgeId) -> meshlib.mrmeshpy.Vector3d

computes directed area of the hole specified by one of its edges with no valid left face (left is hole);
if the hole is planar then returned vector is orthogonal to the plane pointing outside and its magnitude is equal to hole area

topologyFromTriangles(t: meshlib.mrmeshpy.Triangulation, settings: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshBuilder.BuildSettings = MeshBuilder.BuildSettings(), progressCb: meshlib.mrmeshpy.func_bool_from_float = '{}') -> meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshTopology

construct mesh topology from a set of triangles with given ids;
if skippedTris is given then it receives all input triangles not added in the resulting topology

signedDistanceToMesh(mp: meshlib.mrmeshpy.MeshPart, p: meshlib.mrmeshpy.Vector3f, op: meshlib.mrmeshpy.SignedDistanceToMeshOptions) -> float

computes signed distance from point (p) to mesh part (mp) following options (op);
returns std::nullopt if distance is smaller than op.minDist or larger than op.maxDist (except for op.signMode == HoleWindingRule)

